# Getting around in Russian: сле́дующая ста́нция
subtitle: "Get around a Russian city by metro and bus: остано́вка and ста́нция, the переса́дка, the next station, ско́лько е́хать? and вы выхо́дите? on a full bus."
tags: ["russian","metro","bus","getting around","russian travel phrases"]
teaches: ["phrases/travel-phrases","grammar/verbs-of-motion"]
thumb: "band \"Are you getting off?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Telling a story in Russian: снача́ла, пото́м","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/94-russian-narrative.cast"}

## Getting around in Russian: сле́дующая ста́нция
level: basic

